rules.mdc — Interactive Multiplayer Quiz x Pump.fun (React + Node.js)

Goal: Build a fast, legible, production-ready web quiz system that ingests answers via Pump.fun live chat and broadcasts 30s rounds in real time. Clean UX, robust Node backend, Solana token stats, weekly leaderboard + token tips for Top 3.

⸻

0) Tech Decisions (must)
	•	Frontend: React + Vite, TypeScript, TailwindCSS.
	•	State mgmt: Zustand (lightweight), React Query for data fetching.
	•	Realtime: socket.io-client (UI updates). Answers come from Pump.fun chat via server.
	•	Backend: Node.js + TypeScript, Express (REST) + socket.io (WS).
	•	Storage: Redis (round state, rate limits), PostgreSQL or MongoDB (users, weekly scores, logs).
	•	Solana: @solana/web3.js (+ @solana/spl-token later for prize payouts).
	•	Jobs: node-cron or BullMQ for weekly reset & prize distribution.
	•	Lint/Format: ESLint + Prettier + Husky (pre-commit).
	•	Env: .env + Zod schema to validate required vars at boot.

⸻

1) User Stories (acceptance criteria)
	1.	As a visitor, I can see the current question, a 30s countdown, and choices A–D.
	2.	I’m told to answer in live chat (“Type /a, /b, /c, /d in Pump.fun chat”).
	3.	When the round ends, I see the correct answer, winners, and my weekly score.
	4.	I can open Leaderboard to view Top 50 weekly players and search my wallet/name.
	5.	I can open Token page to see Top 10 holders and basic token meta.
	6.	Every week, the leaderboard resets and the Top 3 get token tips (recorded on-chain and visible with tx links).
	7.	The UI is mobile-first, readable, with clear contrasts and no jank < 100ms frame stutters.

⸻

2) Pages & Routes (frontend)
	•	/ → Landing: short how-it-works, Join Game CTA, live token stats tickers (optional).
	•	/game → Live Game: question, 30s timer, choice cards (read-only), status feed.
	•	/leaderboard → Weekly leaderboard + search.
	•	/token/:mint → Token details (Top 10 holders, mint, supply, updates).
	•	/legal → Terms/Privacy.

⸻

3) UI/UX Guidelines
	•	Design tokens (Tailwind):
	•	Primary: #0A2E52 (ink), Accent: #2DB4FF, Surface: #0E1B1F, Muted: #C7D2FE, Success: #22C55E, Danger: #EF4444.
	•	Font: Inter, system fallback.
	•	Layout: max-w 900px centered, generous spacing (8/12/16). Cards with subtle shadow and rounded-2xl.
	•	Countdown: circular progress + numeric seconds. Color shifts 10s → Accent to Danger.
	•	Question: Large, high-contrast. Choices A–D visible but disabled; subtitle text: “Answer in live chat: /a /b /c /d”.
	•	Live feed: vertical list of last 10 events (”@alice answered A”, “Round ended: Correct B”).
	•	Leader row: avatar (initials), name/wallet-short, score badge.
	•	Empty/Loading states: skeletons, spinners, no layout shift.
	•	Accessibility: semantic HTML, aria-live for announcements (round start/end), 44px touch targets.

⸻

4) Client State Model (Zustand)

// ui/store/game.ts
interface RoundState {
  roundId: string | null;
  question: string;
  options: [string, string, string, string];
  correct?: 'A'|'B'|'C'|'D'; // filled after end
  endsAt: number; // ms epoch
  status: 'idle'|'running'|'ended';
  winners: Array<{ id: string; name: string }>; // after end
}


⸻

5) WebSocket Events (contract)

Server → Client
	•	round:start → { id, question, options: [A,B,C,D], endsAt }
	•	round:tick → { now } (optional if client computes)
	•	round:end → { id, correct, winners: [{id,name}], total }
	•	trade:update → { price, vol, tx, ts } (optional showcase)

Client → Server
	•	(none for answers; answers come from Pump.fun chat via server). Optional: client:hello to register UI session.

⸻

6) REST API (contract)
	•	GET /api/leaderboard/weekly?limit=50&cursor= → { items:[{userId,name,score}], nextCursor }
	•	GET /api/token/:mint/top-holders → { holders:[{owner, amount}] }
	•	GET /api/me → returns inferred identity if available (from chat mapping) else null.
	•	GET /api/health → { ok:true, version }

⸻

7) Backend Modules (Node)
	•	src/index.ts → app bootstrap, env validation, HTTP + WS server.
	•	src/ws/index.ts → socket.io setup, broadcast helpers.
	•	src/game/engine.ts → round loop (30s), timers, state, emits.
	•	src/game/answers.ts → Redis sets/hmaps; one-answer-per-round policy.
	•	src/integrations/pumpChat.ts → Your ready WS client goes here. Normalize {roomMint, account, displayName, message} → call answers.ingest().
	•	src/integrations/pumpPortal.ts → optional trade stream to UI.
	•	src/integrations/solana.ts → getTopHolders(mint), rpc client.
	•	src/db → Prisma (Postgres) or Mongoose (Mongo). Tables/collections: users, scoresWeekly, roundLogs, payouts.
	•	src/jobs/weekly.ts → compute Top 3, trigger payouts, reset leaderboard.
	•	src/http/routes.ts → Express routes from API contract.
	•	src/security/rateLimit.ts → IP/wallet flood control.

⸻

8) Data & DB Schema (suggested)

-- Postgres
CREATE TABLE users (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,          -- wallet or hashed chat id
  display_name TEXT,
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE scores_weekly (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,          -- `${week}_${userId}`
  week INT NOT NULL,            -- ISO week number
  user_id TEXT REFERENCES users(id),
  score INT DEFAULT 0,
  updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE TABLE payouts (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  week INT,
  user_id TEXT,
  rank INT,
  amount NUMERIC,
  tx TEXT,                      -- signature
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now()
);

Redis keys
	•	answers:{roundId} → HMAP { userId: 'A'|'B'|'C'|'D' }
	•	answered:{roundId} → SET of userIds (first valid wins)
	•	scores:weekly → HMAP { userId: score } (mirror for speed, then persist to DB)

⸻

9) Round Engine (business rules)
	•	Round length: 30s hard cap.
	•	Cooldown: 5s between rounds.
	•	One valid answer per userId per round.
	•	Scoring: +1 per correct. (allow future weights)
	•	Broadcast schedule: round:start immediately, round:end at T=30s.
	•	Edge cases: if no answers → still round:end with total=0.

⸻

10) Identity & Anti-cheat
	•	Primary identity: wallet public key from chat payload if provided; else stable account id.
	•	Display name: best-effort from chat; sanitize (strip emojis/zero-width, length <= 24).
	•	Rate limits: Max 1 answer per 2s per user; global 30 req/min per IP.
	•	Moderation: strip URLs, ignore messages > 50 chars; accept only a|b|c|d|/a|/b|/c|/d (case-insensitive) as answers.
	•	Logging: persist suspicious activity for audit.

⸻

11) Solana & Payouts (phase 2)
	•	Treasury wallet in .env. Use @solana/spl-token to ensure ATA, then transfer token to winners.
	•	Weekly cron: compute Top 3 from DB; enqueue transfers; record tx signature.
	•	UI displays last week winners with on-chain links.

⸻

12) Question Source & AI
	•	V1: curated JSON bank (medium difficulty, general knowledge/history). Keep source field for transparency.
	•	V2: AI generator service creates distractors; human-in-the-loop approval; cache into questions_approved.
	•	Validation: no ambiguous/dated questions; include updatedAt and region if relevant.

