16) HTTP/WS Skeletons (snippets)

Express routes

router.get('/leaderboard/weekly', ctrl.leaderboard.getWeekly);
router.get('/token/:mint/top-holders', ctrl.token.getTopHolders);
router.get('/health', (_req,res) => res.json({ ok:true, version: process.env.npm_package_version }));

Socket wiring

io.on('connection', (socket) => {
  socket.emit('hello', { t: Date.now() });
});

function broadcastRoundStart(payload) {
  io.emit('round:start', payload);
}
function broadcastRoundEnd(payload) {
  io.emit('round:end', payload);
}


⸻

17) Frontend Components (must-have)
	•	Countdown.tsx: derived from endsAt; updates every 200ms; color thresholds (<=10s danger).
	•	QuestionCard.tsx: question + 4 choices (disabled); helper text to chat answers.
	•	LiveFeed.tsx: last N events; auto-scroll; aria-live="polite".
	•	LeaderRow.tsx: compact row for leaderboard.
	•	TokenHolders.tsx: table of top holders; short addresses; copy btn.

⸻

18) Performance Guidelines
	•	Avoid re-render storms: memoize components, colocate state.
	•	Socket events: debounce UI updates to 10–15 fps if needed.
	•	Code-split routes; prefetch /game on landing CTA hover.
	•	Images/icons: SVG inline, no heavy libs.

⸻

19) Security & Privacy
	•	Never expose treasury keys to frontend. Server-only.
	•	Sanitize all incoming chat display names and messages.
	•	CORS: restrict origins in production.
	•	Rate limit REST and WS connections; ban on abuse.
	•	Telemetry: anonymized metrics only (no PII beyond wallet public key / hashed ids).

⸻

20) QA Checklist (blockers to ship)
	•	Round loop runs stable for 1h (no drift; ends exactly at 30s).
	•	One-answer-per-user enforced.
	•	Leaderboard sorts correctly + pagination works.
	•	Token Top 10 holders endpoint returns within < 1s cached.
	•	Mobile (375px), Tablet (768px), Desktop (1440px) layouts verified.
	•	Accessibility: keyboard focus, aria-live, contrast AA.
	•	Env validation & 500 handler paths covered.

⸻

21) Cursor Tasks (copy-paste to Cursor)

Task: Bootstrap Monorepo
	•	Create apps/web (React + Vite + TS + Tailwind) and apps/api (Express + TS + socket.io).
	•	Add ESLint/Prettier/Husky shared config in packages/.
	•	Implement .env schema validation.

Task: Realtime Game Engine
	•	Implement engine.ts: 30s round tick, broadcast start/end, integrate Redis for answers.
	•	Expose startRoundLoop() from server entry.

Task: Pump.fun Chat Integration
	•	Wire your ready socket client inside integrations/pumpChat.ts.
	•	Normalize payload and call answers.ingest(roundId, userId, displayName, choice).

Task: Token Holders Endpoint
	•	Add GET /api/token/:mint/top-holders using Solana RPC; cache 30s in Redis.

Task: UI
	•	Build /game with Countdown, QuestionCard, LiveFeed and socket connection.
	•	Build /leaderboard with server pagination.

⸻

22) Definition of Done (DoD)
	•	Live demo where two browsers observe the same round; chat answers increment scores correctly; leaderboard updates on refresh.
	•	Token page shows Top 10 holders for configured MINT.
	•	Weekly reset cron can be dry-run and logs intended winners.
	•	Lighthouse perf score ≥ 90 mobile.

⸻

23) Future Work
	•	Prize payouts on-chain (SPL token transfers) with admin dashboard.
	•	OBS overlay mode for streams.
	•	Multi-room support (different mints/rooms).
	•	AI narrated questions (TTS) with low-latency audio injection.

⸻

Notes
	•	You already have the Pump.fun live socket listener. This rules file assumes you will plug it into integrations/pumpChat.ts and emit standardized events to the game engine.
	•	Keep functions pure, isolate IO, and unit-test the engine (deterministic timers via fake clock where possible).

